=== PyFolio tear-sheet meaning (reuse existing metrics) ===
cite: Quantopian pyfolio / pyfolio-reloaded — create_returns_tear_sheet(returns, benchmark_rets=...)
params: same toy pnl at 5 bps; Rf=0; ann=√252
tear_sheet_map (PyFolio-style label → value → how we already compute it)
  Annual return        +0.024600  via mean(daily)×252
  Annual volatility    +0.126000  via std(daily)×√252
  Sharpe ratio         +0.194900  via (mean-Rf)/std×√252
  Max drawdown         -0.091900  via min(nav/peak-1)
  Cumulative return    +0.016700  via final NAV - 1
  Daily VaR (5%)       -0.014978  via empirical 5th pct of daily pnl
  Stability (R^2)      +0.340600  via R² of log-NAV vs time
teach: a returns tear sheet is a dashboard of metrics you already met in returns-vol-corr / this lab — it does not create a new edge; read full sample vs OOS carefully and still apply cost honesty.
benchmark note: tear sheets often take benchmark_rets; compare excess return / beta only when the benchmark is investable and aligned.
